host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The row that owed nothing to anyone, and the first free lift with no answer behind it
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Caravan ladder lift arc, Standfast on reds first, read one council-rota row, sweep the prose Radiant, and send.
think Standfast first. crux/REDS.md reads through %144 with every row carrying its own CLOSED note, and the newest closures name witnesses on metal rather than claims, so no agent-closable red stood open and the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend line rather than from REMEMBER alone. It named read_the_reply as the fall head at 414 -- ten rungs at forty-nine lines over a three-line stub, widening nothing of any kind -- and named mend_the_plan as the carry head returning only 72 behind a seventeen-line signature. Fall orders what a lift returns; carry orders what a family holds. The lap took the fall head.
think Read the harness before the meter, as the arc's own teaching asks. caravan/ladder_checks.rye holds every lifted body as a published function taking the rung as a comptime type parameter, and its three newest -- elder_waits, may_pass, choose_pass -- each document which priced column they paid and how it was answered. That reading set the shape of this lift before the scan was consulted a second time.
think The widening was verified by hand rather than taken from the meter. All nineteen names the body climbs outward for -- max_address_len, address_published, addressable, recounted_to, allay_of, unheard_replies, read_back_in, unread_in, rest_written, rests_rest, rests_answers, allay_refusal, allay_note, allay_holds, rest_published, Allay, Report, RunError, NoteError -- were checked for a pub declaration in each of the ten folding rungs, and every one stood open. None of the ten stands below the fold line either, so nothing was foreclosed by the harness already importing it.
think The eleventh rung stays home on its own merits. caravan/allay.rye writes report_out.read_back directly where the other ten reach the same field through allay_of(report_out), so its body is a different body rather than a copy of this one -- which is exactly what the meter means by declared=11 identical=10.
obs Carry measured 62,334 -> 61,920 after the lift -- exactly 414, the number the scan's own formula returned before the lap began. Three laps running the arithmetic has named the fall before the meter read it, now across three different families and two different stub widths.
obs This is the first row of the arc to have been free of every priced column at once. Every earlier free lift answered a price: a function column answered from underneath, where the helper already stood lifted in the same harness, or an import column answered from above, where the harness binds the module at its own head. This row had nothing to answer, because the arc's own habit of publishing what it reaches had already opened every name before the lap arrived.
obs The finding worth carrying is that a widening price is a fact about where names stand today rather than about the body being lifted. An arc that keeps publishing what it reaches eventually meets rows that cost nothing to free, and the fall queue finds them before the carry queue does.
obs The next head is a genuinely new column rather than a wider old one. asked_of returns 360 over thirty-one rungs, and its widening names a private function in each folding rung beside an equal column of private constants. Neither of this arc's two answers reaches a constant, so the lap that takes that row finds out whether the lift-underneath habit reaches a value as well as a body.
obs The council rota row read this lap was Air and Saturn -- law and boundary. Conway's Law landed directly on the work: the communication channel between sessions is made of files, so lifting fifty copies of a rule into one published body is a Conway move as much as a carry move. Fifty copies are fifty places a future session may quietly come to disagree with itself; one body is one place the disagreement cannot start.
obs One honest operator note rather than a tree red. The first choir run went RED on tools/caravan_queue_witness.rish, and that witness reads GREEN alone -- because a rung witness was started by hand while the suite was mid-run, and the two shared a build output path. The shape is already booked and archived as the shared-output-path pair (REDS rows 133-134), so it is named here rather than re-booked. The choir was re-run with nothing else on the bench.
loom witness=caravan_ladder_carry_scan carry_before=62334 carry_after=61920 fall=414 folding=10 body_lines=49 stub_lines=3 bodies=18191 modules=110
